            "evidence": [
              "ci.yml: both Deadcode steps capture output with out=$(go run ... -test ...). Actions runs bash with -e, so a failed go run (unresolvable version, type error) fails the assignment and the step. Any printed line also fails the step explicitly. This covers the fact that deadcode exits 0 when it reports findings. The tui step passes -tags backend, consistent with its vet and staticcheck steps.",
              "engine/settings/projection.go and engine/skills/approval_write.go: the deleted ProjectionHookEntries and BaselineLintDecision are, per the task log, reported by deadcode -test as having no callers. BaselineLintDecisionAgainst keeps the same logic and signature, so behavior is unchanged. The approve.go change is a comment only.",
              "engine/skills/manifest_paths_test.go: the test resolves every manifest row through ResolveRoutes and stats RepoSource, falling back to RepoRel. It fails with a message naming the row, route and path. It also guards against an empty manifest. The task log reports a negative probe with injected stale rows. I could not see repoRoot, ReadManifestRows or ResolveRoutes in this patch, so I assume they exist as the log describes.",
              "tui/backend_tag_test.go: testFileReader now recognizes a command that has -test and a deadcode package field as 'deadcode'. The table-driven test covers positive cases, including the command-substitution form, and keeps the negative case with no -test. The TUI job test now requires a deadcode step. The new use of slices depends on an import I cannot see in this diff; the task log reports the tui tests green.",
              "Residual risk, not attributable to a defect in the diff: the engine job's Go 1.21 setup relies on toolchain auto-switching for x/tools v0.48.0. The task log acknowledges this and says the first CI run is the proof."
